 "text": "Hey there, how are you doing? You can use a deep cable channel and sit on chair as the base of each keyhold. Alternatively, run each cable up a wall and wrap them with cable ties. Run each cable up a wall and wrap them with cable ties, so they don't turn into a nest. Or hang them out of the way with wall plugs on them. Not really. A deep channel keeps them out of reach, running up goes where they go, and plugs un plugged cables can go in the cupboard. Then turn it right down and keep it plugged in, or hang the laptop from wall plugs with a cable tie. Keep them on the desk and use wall plugs, or run them up and wrap if you use the desk every day.",
